Given matrix  A = \left[ {\matrix{ 0 & 2  \cr k & { - 1}  \cr

} } \right] 

${A^4} + 3IA = 2I \Rightarrow {A^4} = 2I - 3A$

Also characteristic equation of A is $|A - \lambda I|\, = 0 $\Rightarrow \left| {\matrix{
   {0 - \lambda } & 2  \cr 
   k & { - 1 - \lambda }  \cr 

 } } \right| = 0 

$\Rightarrow \lambda  + {\lambda ^2} - 2k = 0 \Rightarrow A + {A^2} = 2K.I \Rightarrow {A^2} = 2KI - A \Rightarrow {A^4} = 4{K^2}I + {A^2} - 4AK$

Put ${A^2} = 2KI - A$

and ${A^4} = 2I - 3A 2I - 3A = 4{K^2}I + 2KI - A - 4AK \Rightarrow I(2 - 2K - 4{K^2}) = A(2 - 4K) \Rightarrow  - 2I(2{K^2} + K - 1) = 2A(1 - 2K) \Rightarrow  - 2I(2K - 1)(K + 1) = 2A(1 - 2K) \Rightarrow (2K - 1)(2A) - 2I(2K - 1)(K + 1) = 0 \Rightarrow (2K - 1)[2A - 2I(K + 1)] = 0 \Rightarrow K = \frac{1}{2}$

